#: ../../technical/articles/100-storage-lifecycle-management-and-ledger-import-diagnostics.md:12
msgid "Capabilities and mechanisms"
msgstr "Képességek és mechanizmusok"

#: ../../technical/articles/100-storage-lifecycle-management-and-ledger-import-diagnostics.md:14
msgid ""
"Storage management derives its inventory, health check, initialization, "
"and reclaim targets from the shared storage taxonomy. The inventory "
"aggregates internal locations into stable public areas and reports "
"occupancy, durable/reclaimable/mixed disposition, number of resolved "
"paths, immediate entry count, and disk footprint. A bucket-scoped "
"location is `UNRESOLVED` when no active profile is selected, distinct "
"from a path that was checked and found absent. Tree inspection is read-"
"only, considers only configured root-scoped locations, and distinguishes "
"a missing directory from a normal absent file-valued leaf. Permission "
"drift is reported only where root mode bits are enforceable; the report "
"says explicitly when that check is not available. Taxonomy-backed "
"inventory (`src/cadrumo/application/storage_management/service.py`), "
"read-only tree inspection "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/storage_management/service.py`), public report "
"contracts (`src/cadrumo/application/storage_management/models.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/100-storage-lifecycle-management-and-ledger-import-diagnostics.md:16
msgid ""
"Initialization delegates to the same tree materializer used by runtime "
"bootstrap and reports only directories created during that invocation. It"
" does not clear or recreate existing storage. Reclaim derives eligible "
"locations from the declared RETENTION, ROTATION, and TTL lifecycles, "
"refusing durable state and exports. Before any deletion it selects "
"minimal outermost paths, validates all candidate lifecycles and root "
"scope, checks for protected declared descendants, rejects link-like or "
"out-of-root targets, counts the current entries, and requires explicit "
"`confirmed=True`. Removal keeps failures in the report and avoids "
"following symlink or junction entries. Lifecycle policy and init "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/storage_management/service.py`), reclaim "
"preflight and confirmation "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/storage_management/service.py`), all-target "
"preflight (`src/cadrumo/application/storage_management/service.py`), live"
" path containment and link handling "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/storage_management/service.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/100-storage-lifecycle-management-and-ledger-import-diagnostics.md:18
msgid ""
"Area-level occupancy is derived from the strongest state among its "
"selected paths: populated outranks empty, empty outranks absent, and "
"unresolved is returned only when nothing could be resolved. Directory "
"occupancy counts immediate children; file occupancy distinguishes zero-"
"byte from non-empty files. Nested paths are reduced to unique outermost "
"roots before calculating entry totals or size, so one cache tree is not "
"counted repeatedly through its descendants. Occupancy precedence and area"
" aggregation (`src/cadrumo/application/storage_management/service.py`), "
"minimal-path and footprint handling "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/storage_management/service.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/100-storage-lifecycle-management-and-ledger-import-diagnostics.md:20
msgid ""
"Ledger import preview emits strict, typed diagnostics for parser-empty "
"input, duplicates or ID collisions, calendar gaps, and an optional "
"original-file check. A single pure classifier is shared with the "
"persistence path so preview and actual import use the same decision. A "
"previously stored fingerprint is skipped; a repeated fingerprint within "
"the current batch imports both rows and produces an advisory; a repeated "
"transaction ID in the batch is skipped because it would overwrite the "
"earlier catalogue key. The ordering gives stored duplicates precedence, "
"then ID collisions, then intra-batch fingerprint repeats. Shared row "
"verdict "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/transactions/import_classification.py`), "
"classification order "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/transactions/import_classification.py`), "
"diagnostic preview flow "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/transactions/import_diagnostics.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/100-storage-lifecycle-management-and-ledger-import-diagnostics.md:22
msgid ""
"The preview requires exactly one caller-derived, direction-qualified "
"import fingerprint per raw row, compares those against existing catalogue"
" fingerprints, and reports imported/skipped counts with diagnostic "
"records. It processes rows in input order, collects their dates, and "
"warns when adjacent sorted dates are more than 35 days apart. A present "
"original-source path gets an informational diagnostic; an unreadable path"
" gets a warning. Diagnostic kinds and severities are closed enums, source"
" locators are trimmed and bounded, and construction verifies the "
"translation key has an authoritative Spanish rendering. Row processing "
"and gap checks "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/transactions/import_diagnostics.py`), original-"
"file check "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/transactions/import_diagnostics.py`), "
"diagnostic validation "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/transactions/diagnostics.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/100-storage-lifecycle-management-and-ledger-import-diagnostics.md:24
msgid "Knowledge, security, and implementation assessment"
msgstr "Tudás-, biztonsági és megvalósítási értékelés"

#: ../../technical/articles/100-storage-lifecycle-management-and-ledger-import-diagnostics.md:26
msgid ""
"Storage decisions rely on the canonical taxonomy and current settings, "
"plus live filesystem observations. Reclaim selects no arbitrary user-"
"supplied path: area and lifecycle determine candidates. Durable "
"namespaces and key material are explicitly outside the reclaimable set, "
"while symlink/junction and containment checks guard the destructive "
"boundary. The explicit confirmation check lives in the service, so a "
"programmatic caller receives the same confirmation requirement as the "
"CLI. Inventory aggregation avoids double-counting nested paths and "
"reports unresolved bucket paths honestly. Reclaimable lifecycle set "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/storage_management/service.py`), root-scoped "
"aggregate calculation "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/storage_management/service.py`), occupancy "
"semantics (`src/cadrumo/application/storage_management/service.py`), "
"service-level confirmation error "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/storage_management/errors.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/100-storage-lifecycle-management-and-ledger-import-diagnostics.md:28
msgid ""
"The import preview’s evidence is limited to parser-provided rows, the "
"current catalogue, their fingerprints, and source paths. It does not "
"persist records or mutate the catalogue; persistence, FX normalization, "
"and bucket-event emission are delegated to the ledger application layer. "
"Reusing the classifier avoids a previous preview/import disagreement that"
" could have skipped a genuine repeated movement and understated totals. "
"One terminology limit remains: the “verified original file” path check is"
" based on existence/readability, not comparison of original bytes against"
" the parsed source. Diagnostic-only package boundary "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/transactions/__init__.py`), original path "
"existence behavior "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/transactions/import_diagnostics.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/100-storage-lifecycle-management-and-ledger-import-diagnostics.md:30
msgid ""
"One destructive-boundary caveat is worth testing. Reclaim validates each "
"target before counting and deleting; it also rechecks link types at "
"removal of individual entries. Filesystem paths can still change between "
"those checks and a later recursive removal, so the concrete threat model "
"should confirm whether a concurrent replacement can redirect deletion "
"after containment was established. This static pass does not establish "
"race-free deletion. The inventory also degrades unreadable enumeration "
"and sizing to zero after debug logging; the resulting empty/zero report "
"is not a distinct permission-failure state, so operators could mistake "
"incomplete measurement for genuinely empty storage. Preflight and later "
"deletion (`src/cadrumo/application/storage_management/service.py`), best-"
"effort size and entry counts "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/storage_management/service.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/100-storage-lifecycle-management-and-ledger-import-diagnostics.md:32
msgid "Dependencies and follow-up"
msgstr "Függőségek és további vizsgálatok"

#: ../../technical/articles/100-storage-lifecycle-management-and-ledger-import-diagnostics.md:34
msgid ""
"Trace taxonomy categories to their concrete resolved paths and encrypted "
"storage adapter, and verify the destructive adapter behavior on POSIX "
"symlinks and Windows junctions under concurrent filesystem changes. Check"
" whether unreadable inventory paths should surface an issue instead of a "
"zero measurement. Follow the import classifier into the persisting ledger"
" action and confirm it updates both batch fingerprint and transaction-ID "
"sets in the same way. Test stored duplicates, repeated fingerprints that "
"import as two movements, ID collisions that skip, malformed fingerprint "
"counts, the 35-day gap boundary, missing original files, and storage "
"confirmation/refusal for mixed areas. No assigned tests or filesystem "
"mutation were performed."
msgstr ""

